Z||000000||strdream||12-05-2000||02:16 PM||||I am looking for a service manual for the Fiero.<P>I have one in hand "Pontiac 1985 Preliminary Service Information - Fiero".<P>I look in the table of contents and find a lot of asterisks next to several section titles, at the bottom of the page reads "* Refer to 1984 Fiero Service Manual".<P>So I guess I need another service manual that is comprehensive.  Is there a good place to look.<P>Thank you!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||12-05-2000||02:41 PM||||Try the <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>FieroStore</A><P>Click Online Store and acroll to find literature/service manuals.  I was just looking at these the other day.<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||12-05-2000||05:46 PM||||I would suggest that you look on eBay for the factory manuals.  There are usually several for each year (except 88's) on at once.  They are usually far cheaper than the new copies from the Fiero Store or directly from Helms.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||12-06-2000||09:03 AM||||Ross,<P>I would definitely not go with anything less than a Helms manual.  I have seen all the others and they just don't stack up.  The only problem is that the 88's are pricey, but all other years are often bought new for less than on ebay.  <P>Go to <A HREF="http://www.helm.com" TARGET=_blank>www.helm.com</A>   I bought my 85 manual for around $65 which included shipping just over a year ago.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
